Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:39:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Recolor Calendar page and remove dead day-selection CSS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Calendar page's header cards were already correctly rebranded
(brand/accent gradients), but the trip cards inside the day preview
panel, the filter toggle buttons, and the empty/loading states
underneath were still saturated with raw emerald/blue/purple —
the pre-rebrand palette. Recolored all of it to brand/accent tokens,
consistent with the rest of the page.

Also found and removed ~90 lines of dead CSS in an inline <style>
block: react-day-picker's day-cell classes (rdp-button,
rdp-day_selected, rdp-day_today, rdp-day_outside) and a custom
day-badge class were all styled with hardcoded hex colors (emerald/
cyan for selection, amber for "today", a pulsing red badge) — but
this component's custom Day renderer replaces each day cell with its
own <div className="day-content">, discarding whatever className
react-day-picker would have assigned. None of those classes ever
reach the DOM, so none of that CSS has taken effect since whenever
this custom renderer was introduced — confirmed empirically, the
live selected-day styling already comes entirely from dayRenderer's
own Tailwind classes (bg-ceylon-green), matching what's on screen
today. Left the CSS rules that do still apply (nav buttons, weekday
header, day-content's own layout rule) alone.

Also removed client/src/components/EventCalendar.tsx — an earlier,
unrelated calendar component that's never imported anywhere.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
